cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, cite the frozen release you used by its version DOI, not the live site,
  which is rebuilt every week. Also cite the CCS '25 dataset it derives from, listed under references.
type: dataset
title: "APT Explorer: A Merged, Provenance-Tracked Dataset of APT Actors and Reports"
abstract: >-
  APT Explorer merges advanced persistent threat (APT) actor records from MITRE ATT&CK, the MISP
  galaxy, ETDA Threat Group Cards and Malpedia, and links them to public threat reports from the
  CCS '25 lab dataset, ORKL, Malpedia's library, The DFIR Report and three vendor blogs. Every
  report records the basis of its date, and every actor merge keeps its evidence. The data in data/
  is a derived dataset; docs/datasheet.md documents its composition, provenance and known errors.
authors:
  - family-names: Ennis
    given-names: Garrett
    affiliation: "SecAI Lab, Sungkyunkwan University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hi-im-pod/apt-explorer"
url: "https://hi-im-pod.github.io/apt-explorer/"
license:
  - CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
  - MIT
keywords:
  - advanced persistent threat
  - cyber threat intelligence
  - threat actor attribution
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - dataset
